        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "f488439a-eebd-5250-828f-c17c01d391d3",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Companies: Dain Rauscher Wessels, Berenberg Bank, Royal Bank of Canada\n- People: John G. Taft\n- Places: Minneapolis, Minnesota, Hamburg\n- Topics: Brokerage, investment banking, private banking, acquisitions, company origins\n\nFacts:\n- Berenberg Bank was founded in Hamburg in 1590 by the Belgian-origin Berenberg family.\n- Dain Rauscher Wessels traced its origins to smaller regional securities firms founded in the 1920s and 1930s.\n- Dain Rauscher Wessels was a brokerage and investment banking firm based in Minneapolis, Minnesota.\n- John G. Taft’s unit at Dougherty was later acquired by Dain Rauscher.\n- Royal Bank of Canada acquired Dain Rauscher in 2001, and John G. Taft then began working with Royal Bank of Canada.",
